It is the name of my inn, the 'Star of Allah.'	這是我旅店的名字，「阿拉之星」。
The name of my inn is 'The Star of Allah.' Caupona means inn, habib.	我旅店的名字是「阿拉之星」。Caupona 的意思就是旅店，朋友。
I do my best to keep them out of my inn.	我盡力不讓牠們靠近我的旅店。
If I only had a broom, I would help you.	若我有把掃帚，我便會幫你。
I cannot help you with that, but you can surely stay at my inn.	那件事我幫不上忙，但你儘管留宿在我的旅店。
As much as I would like to take your money, I cannot think of serving you until I can clean my inn.	我雖然很想收你的錢，但旅店未清理乾淨之前，我實在無法招待你。
I could never take your money, habibi. I am in your debt.	我絕不能收你的錢，朋友。我還欠著你的情。
But he has the broom.	但掃帚在他手上。
I will never part with this broom!	這把掃帚，我絕不會放手！
Would that I HAD a broom!	但願我真的有把掃帚！
Your generosity does you credit, but if I could have anything, I would only desire a broom.	你的慷慨令人敬佩，但若要我說想要什麼，我只求一把掃帚。
I could not take another gift. I am in your debt already.	我不能再收你的禮物了，我已經欠你人情。
Perhaps later, when I recover my losses from being closed for so long.	或許等日後吧，等我把歇業許久的損失彌補回來再說。
One of the merchants on this street could doubtless sell you that.	這條街上的商人，想必有人能賣你那個。
Odd that the inn should be locked.	旅店竟然上了鎖，真是奇怪。
It is still locked.	依然上著鎖。
Achmed is surely busy sweeping his floor. I doubt he will answer you.	阿賀密德想必正忙著掃地，我看他不會理你。
I am not open for business. Go away.	我沒有營業，走開。
I cannot open my shop. For weeks I have been without a broom and now I am overcome with filth. All because my cousin, Tariq, is angry with me and will not sell me a broom for any amount of coin. And I offered good money just for a broom!	我沒法開店。這幾個星期我都沒有掃帚，如今店裡髒亂不堪，全是因為我表弟泰利克在生我的氣，無論出多少錢都不肯賣我一把掃帚。我可是出了好價錢，就只為求一把掃帚啊！
Do not blame me that I cannot offer you rest and food. Talk to Tariq, who has the stubbornness of a goat. He certainly will not talk to me!	我沒法供你歇腳用膳，這可不能怪我。去找泰利克談吧，那人跟山羊一樣倔強。他肯定是不會跟我說話的！
I am sorry, but without a broom, I cannot open for business.	很抱歉，沒有掃帚，我沒法開店營業。
Did you want something else? I thought you did.	你還想要別的嗎？我還以為你有事。
Welcome, habibi, welcome! Come in!	歡迎，朋友，歡迎！請進！
Until then, may I offer you the hospitality of my humble inn. Excuse the mess on the floor. I will clean it while you eat and drink at no charge.	在那之前，且容我以寒舍略盡地主之誼。地上凌亂，還請見諒，你儘管吃喝，我這就分文不收，一邊替你打掃。
You have eaten well and spent a restless night being bitten by bedbugs and dreaming about Camelot, Gwenhyver, and the Grail.	你飽餐一頓，卻在床蝨叮咬與夢見肯萊特、昆海兒與聖杯之中，度過了一夜輾轉難眠。
 A new sense of urgency fills you. The land and the people will not survive much longer unless you can find the Grail!	 一股新的迫切感湧上心頭。除非你能尋得聖杯，否則這片土地與人民撐不了多久了！
Good, I am glad you have the sense not to dally at an inn when your entire kingdom is at stake.	很好，你的王國正處存亡之際，你懂得不在旅店裡蹉跎，這讓我甚感欣慰。
I can see why you did not remain. You have gotten more flea bites from this brief visit than in all your years in Camelot.	我明白你為何沒有留下。這趟短暫停留，你被跳蚤咬的次數，竟比你在肯萊特這些年加起來還多。
Do you think you could possibly stop blundering around terrifying the natives long enough to do what you are supposed to be doing?	你能不能別再橫衝直撞驚嚇當地百姓，好好去做你該做的事？
How clever of you to somehow convince Tariq to sell the broom. Here, I gladly give you a dirham for it.	你竟有辦法說服泰利克賣出掃帚，真是聰明。來，我樂意付你一枚銀幣。
Ya'Allah! You have managed to part Tariq from his broom. And you give this to me? But surely...why, this can only mean it is an offering of peace from my cousin through you. He has forgiven me!	阿拉在上！你竟讓泰利克交出了他的掃帚。而你把它給了我？這……這只能說明一件事，這是我表弟藉你之手送來的和解之禮。他原諒我了！
Allah bless you, habibi! You have brought my cousin and me together in kinship again. Even though I see you are an infidel, I pray you shall one day know the ecstasy of Paradise!	願阿拉保佑你，朋友！你讓我與表弟重修舊好。雖然我看得出你是異教徒，我仍祈願你有朝一日能得知天堂的至樂！
There is nothing to see.	此處無物可看。
Across the street is an inn.	街對面是一間旅店。
There is some sort of antiquities shop and a butcher's shop.	這裡有間古物店和一間肉舖。
I have the most profound suspicion that Ismail will not return.	我深深懷疑艾思美不會再回來了。
He has vanished into his back room.	他已躲進裡屋去了。
The dog looks like it is well fed from the butcher's scraps.	這隻狗看來吃肉舖的剩肉吃得很好。
Nice try, but I do not think that being nice to Fawaz's dog will do anything to improve Fawaz's temper.	想得美，但我看討好法瓦茲的狗，對法瓦茲的脾氣是不會有什麼幫助的。
Do not bother the dog, he may bite.	別招惹那條狗，牠會咬人。
Would you buy a used chariot from this man?	你會向這種人買二手戰車嗎？
It loosely translates as "Ismail, King of Antiquities". The rest is Arabic and Hebrew graffiti.	大略譯來是「古物之王艾思美」。其餘則是阿拉伯文與希伯來文的塗鴉。
Alas, I have let my Greek fade with disuse and cannot translate.	可惜我的希臘文久未使用，早已生疏，譯不出來。
You should recognize the countenance of the greatest of Roman generals, Julius Caesar.	你應當認得出這副面容，那是羅馬最偉大的將領，儒略·凱撒。
It is pitch black inside.	裡頭一片漆黑。
He has nothing displayed except a Roman bust. Behind that is only a short, empty hall leading to a door. He must keep his antiquities locked in another room.	他店裡除了一尊羅馬胸像外，什麼也沒陳列。胸像後方只是一條通往門口的短短空廊。他的古物想必都鎖在另一間房裡。
Ismail's shop is closed.	艾思美的店關著門。
There are no symbols on the antiquities shop.	古物店上沒有任何符號。
There are no wares in sight. He must keep them in a back room.	不見任何貨物，想必都收在裡屋。
Truly if I could have anything in the world, I would have your money. Yes, that is what I most desire. Your money.	說真的，若這世上能任我挑一物，我要的就是你的錢。是的，那正是我最渴望的——你的錢。
Chas V'Chalila! What possessed me to say such a thing?! Forgive me, habibi. I meant to say that I have a special on saint's relics today. Reasonable prices!	天哪，萬萬不可！我這是鬼迷心竅，怎麼會說出這種話？！原諒我，朋友。我是想說，今天聖徒聖物特價，價錢公道！
My storehouse of relics is a miracle unto itself! If it is holy, I will have it.	我的聖物庫本身便是一則奇蹟！只要是神聖之物，我這裡應有盡有。
Ahalan, habibi. I am Ismail and within my vaults I have wonders, I have miracles, I have relics of the holy saints and prophets.	你好，朋友。我是艾思美，我的寶庫裡有奇珍、有奇蹟，還有聖徒與先知的聖物。
I have blood of the prophet Mohammed! Hairs from the beard of Guruka Singh! Fingerbones of the saints! A sliver from what the Christians call the True Cross!	我有先知穆罕默德的血！有古魯卡·辛格鬍鬚上的毛髮！有聖徒的指骨！還有一片基督徒稱為真十字架的碎片！
A relic for you today, perhaps? I have a special on saint's fingerbones.	今天要不要來件聖物？聖徒指骨正在特價。
No need to yell, habibi. I am right here.	不必喊叫，朋友，我就在這兒。
Habibi, you accidentally closed your purse without giving me money.	朋友，你不小心把錢囊闔上了，卻沒給我錢。
Buying one relic from this fraud is more than enough.	跟這個騙子買一件聖物就已經夠了。
Keep counting, habibi, keep counting.	繼續數吧，朋友，繼續數。
What do you wish to buy, habibi?	你想買什麼，朋友？
Sorry, I am all out of grails today. Try me again in a few weeks. Something is bound to turn up.	抱歉，聖杯今天賣完了。過幾週再來看看，總會有貨進來的。
Ah, well, the truth is I am forbidden by law to sell relics of the Great Prophet Mohammed. But I have a special on saints' relics.	啊，其實吧，律法禁止我販售大先知穆罕默德的聖物。不過聖徒聖物正在特價。
That is rare and valuable. Have you ever tried to shave a Sikh? It is most dangerous. Normally, I would ask no less than 10 dinars! But for you, only 4 dinars.	那件可是稀世珍寶。你可曾試過替錫克教徒剃鬚？那是極其危險之事。照理我開價絕不會低於十枚金幣！但看在你的份上，只要四枚金幣。
I sell holy fingerbones! Not fingernails. Of course, for the right price, it could be arranged.	我賣的是神聖的指骨！不是指甲。當然，價錢談得攏的話，指甲也不是不能安排。
Do I look like a pig-headed Nubian? Go next door.	我看起來像個跟豬一樣倔強的努比亞人嗎？去隔壁吧。
He is a bad-tempered, pig-headed Nubian? Ah, but you should see his daughter!	他是個脾氣壞、跟豬一樣倔強的努比亞人？啊，但你真該見見他的女兒！
Saint Galahad? Did you wish a relic of Saint Galahad? I can sell you one, only 2 dirhams.	聖葛拉漢？你想要聖葛拉漢的聖物嗎？我可以賣你一件，只要兩枚銀幣。
Ahhh, this is an authentic bust of the great Julius Caesar. Pure marble. Only 5 dinars.	啊，這可是偉大的儒略·凱撒的真品胸像，純大理石打造，只要五枚金幣。
I doubt that it is worth any price that this crook asks for it.	我看這騙子開的價錢，那東西根本不值。
I sell antiquities from the holy land. Holy relics and holy fingerbones!	我賣的是聖地古物。神聖聖物與神聖指骨！
I am the king of antiquities! No one can beat my selection or prices!	我是古物之王！我的貨色與價錢，無人能及！
Thief? Heh-heh, that is a harsh word. I am an honest merchant, that I can assure you.	小偷？呵呵，這話說得太重了。我是個誠實的商人，這點我敢保證。
You are in the wrong place. I deal in antiquities only.	你找錯地方了，我只做古物買賣。
Do not worry about that, habib. My relics, though, are something to talk about!	那件事不必擔心，朋友。不過我的聖物，倒是值得一談！
Please keep it, habibi. I do not get along well with animals.	留著吧，朋友，我跟動物向來合不來。
That is like selling bricks to the Bedouin. I have a room full of relics. Want to buy another?	這就像賣磚頭給貝都因人一樣。我這一屋子都是聖物，還想再買一件嗎？
I cannot say that what you offer is entirely without interest, but it does not fit my speciality.	我不能說你這東西全無價值，但它不合我的專門。
What? You want nothing in return? Is this a trick? Nobody gives away something for nothing. No, I will not take it.	什麼？你什麼都不要？這是什麼把戲？天下沒有白白送人東西的事。不，我不會收下。
Please do. I hate that dog.	請便，我討厭那條狗。
This man is unfamiliar with the concept of cleanliness. He has the aroma of a billy goat.	這人似乎不懂什麼叫乾淨，身上一股公山羊的氣味。
Brilliant move, Arthur. The sight of your sword has sent him into hiding in his back room.	好一招，亞瑟。你亮出劍來，把他嚇得躲進裡屋去了。
He is an extraordinarily mean-looking Nubian.	他是個相貌異常兇惡的努比亞人。
"Tabulae Lanius" is a term meaning "butcher", though more literally from the Latin it is "butcher's block". I cannot read the Hebrew graffiti above the door.	「Tabulae Lanius」意為「屠夫」，但按拉丁文直譯則是「屠案」。門上方的希伯來文塗鴉，我讀不懂。
It is a symbol unknown to me. It looks like a flying eye.	這是個我不認得的符號，看起來像一隻長了翅膀的眼睛。
That is quite a large goat.	那是頭相當大的山羊。
There are three chickens hung upon hooks.	鉤子上掛著三隻雞。
There is one leg of lamb hanging on a hook.	鉤子上掛著一條羊腿。
He has sold all of his lamb.	他的羊肉已經賣完了。
Beware of that cleaver, Arthur. I fear the Nubian may use it on more than animal flesh.	小心那把剁肉刀，亞瑟。我擔心那努比亞人動起刀來，恐怕不只對付牲畜的肉。
It is dark inside. You can see nothing.	裡頭一片昏暗，什麼也看不見。
You already are.	你已經是了。
The butcher has sold his stock of meat for the day.	屠夫今天的存貨已經賣完了。
He has a goat, a leg of lamb and chickens hanging in his shop.	他店裡掛著一頭山羊、一條羊腿和幾隻雞。
If you have come back for more meat, you are out of luck. I have sold it all.	你若是回來買肉，那可不巧，我已經賣光了。
Be gone, heathen. I do not like the look of you and I serve only who I please and today it does not please me to serve anyone.	走開，異教徒。我不喜歡你這副模樣，我只招待我樂意招待的人，而今天我誰都不樂意招待。
Do you wonder why I am angry? It is the stink of fish I must endure every day. The foul, damnable stink of fish would drive any man to fury!	你想知道我為何動怒？那是因為我天天得忍受那股魚腥味。這惡臭該死的魚腥味，換作誰都會被逼瘋！
No-one will ever know a day's peace from me for as long as I smell that stinking fish! A curse upon that fishmonger!	只要我還聞得到那股腥臭的魚味，誰都休想從我這兒得半日安寧！詛咒那個賣魚的！
Ya'Allah! The wind blows sweet today. As for you, you look like a foreign heathen, but if you have good coin I will sell to you.	阿拉在上！今天風吹得挺舒暢。至於你，看起來像個外邦異教徒，但你若有好錢，我照樣賣你。
Put up your weapon, infidel dog, or I will call the city guard. And I will chop up whatever pieces of you they leave behind.	收起你的武器，異教狗，否則我便叫城中衛兵來。他們留下的殘軀，我還會拿去剁碎。
He is not for sale.	他不賣。
Touch my dog and you die, infidel.	敢碰我的狗，你就死定了，異教徒。
GUARDS!	衛兵！
Mercenaries chop you up here.	傭兵們就在這裡把你剁成碎塊。
I told you to be gone! I do not want your money or your business.	我叫你走開！我不要你的錢，也不做你的生意。
I am not amused, stranger. Either do business or get lost.	我可沒興致陪你玩，陌生人。要嘛做生意，要嘛滾開。
You are beginning to annoy me again, little man. Go away.	你又開始惹我不耐了，小子。走開。
I do not bargain. Pay my price or be gone.	我不還價。照我的價錢付，不然就走人。
So, do you want to buy something? Speak up!	那麼，你到底要不要買東西？說話啊！
Stop bothering me!	別煩我了！
Are you trying to insult me, infidel?! How dare you suggest I would touch an unclean meat!	你是想羞辱我嗎，異教徒？！你竟敢暗示我會碰不潔的肉！
They are already spoken for by regular customers.	那些已經被老主顧訂走了。
That was only brought to me for butchering by a customer. It is not mine to sell.	那只是有位客人送來讓我宰殺的，不是我的東西，不能賣你。
In Jerusalem?!	在耶路撒冷？！
What would you do with an entire large leg of lamb, Arthur?	你要一整條大羊腿做什麼，亞瑟？
The whole leg is 5 dinars, but I will sell a single cut for 6 fals.	整條羊腿要五枚金幣，但單獨一塊肉我可以賣你六枚銅幣。
I have goat, lamb, and chicken.	我這裡有山羊肉、羊肉和雞肉。
I feed him scraps and he guards my shop. Dogs are far more trustworthy than men.	我拿剩肉餵牠，牠替我看店。狗可比人可靠多了。
Do not even think about my daughter, you foreign swine!	別打我女兒的主意，你這外邦畜生！
Bah, he is crook. All merchants are crooks. I am the only honest man here.	哼，他是個騙子。這裡的商人個個都是騙子，只有我是誠實人。
Pretty dumb you are, if you do not know the sign of a butcher's shop.	連肉舖的招牌都認不出來，你還真是遲鈍。
Bah, no thief dares to rob me!	哼，沒有哪個小偷敢來搶我！
Can you not read? I am a butcher.	你不識字嗎？我是個屠夫。
You annoy me, little man. Go away.	你惹我不耐了，小子。走開。
If you have money, fine. If you do not have money, go somewhere else. I do not buy or trade.	你若有錢，好說。沒錢的話，去別處吧。我不買東西，也不以物易物。
Have you ever tried to eat mule meat? Very tough. But I hear Mohammed is looking for a pack mule, if he has not already left on his trip.	你吃過騾肉嗎？肉硬得很。不過我聽說穆罕默德正在找一頭馱騾，前提是他還沒動身上路。
Is that some piece of Ismail's junk? You bought that? You infidels are dumber than I thought.	那是艾思美賣的破爛玩意兒嗎？你居然買了？你們這些異教徒，比我想的還蠢。
I do not take gifts from strangers.	我不收陌生人的禮物。
I am not sure which smell is stronger: Fawaz or the meat.	我分不清是法瓦茲身上，還是那些肉，味道比較重。
The building is but one floor with no other entrances.	這棟建築只有一層樓，沒有其他入口。
This house sits at the end of the street, abutting an ancient wall. There is but one door.	這棟房子坐落在街道盡頭，緊鄰一道古牆，只有一扇門。
